@startuml catalogue-model-class
' The catalogue's conceptual model (class view), revision 2 (2026-10-27, owner's review).
' Published in docs/catalogue-architecture.md; copied from the restructure-and-evaluate-catalogue
' EPIC's inputs/2026-10-27-catalogue-model.class.puml (that copy is the dated record).
' Lanes (top to bottom): distribution, knowledge, action, external, intent, assurance.

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #546E7A
skinparam ArrowFontColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowFontSize 10
skinparam ClassBorderColor #455A64
skinparam ClassAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam PackageBorderColor #90A4AE
skinparam PackageFontSize 14
skinparam PackageFontStyle bold
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7
skinparam NoteBorderColor #FBC02D
hide empty members
hide circle

title Skillery catalogue: conceptual model (rev. 2, YAGNI-trimmed)

package "1. Distribution: what gets installed" <<Rectangle>> #E3F2FD {
  class Catalogue #BBDEFB {
    version
  }
  class Bundle #BBDEFB {
    name
    description
    requires
  }
  class Binding #BBDEFB {
    file
  }
  class ConfigItem <<later>> #90CAF9 {
    kind : hook, command, rule, setting
    intent
    renderedPerCli
  }
}

package "2. Knowledge: what agents know" <<Rectangle>> #E8F5E9 {
  class Skill #C8E6C9 {
    name
    description
    kind : method, foundation, tool, domain, ...
    posture : reusable, profiled, precise
    facets : six values, see facets.yaml
  }
  class Resource #C8E6C9 {
    kind : reference, asset, script, example
    scope : private, shared
    path
  }
  class ToolPolicy #A5D6A7 {
    allowed
    disallowed
  }
}

package "3. Action: what agents do and where" <<Rectangle>> #FFF3E0 {
  class Agent #FFE0B2 {
    name
    description
    type : delegated, lead, scheduled, partner, open
    mode : primary, subagent, both (derived from type)
    model
    facets : six values, see facets.yaml
  }
  class DispatchContract #FFE0B2 {
    needs
    returns
    sideEffects
    refuses
  }
  class Runtime <<new>> #FFCC80 {
    kind : cli, desktop, server, local-cron
    trigger
    evidenceLog
    resultHome
  }
}

package "4. External: what it relies on" <<Rectangle>> #FCE4EC {
  class ExternalDependency #F8BBD0 {
    kind : plugin, skill, cli-tool, mcp-server, service, framework
    source
    pin : version, commit, hash
    provenance
    installCheck
    cliSupport : claude, opencode, both
  }
  class MemoryStore <<new>> #F48FB1 {
    kind : odoo, confluence, vault, cognee
  }
}

package "5. Intent: why it exists" <<Rectangle>> #F3E5F5 {
  class UseCase <<new>> #CE93D8 {
    id : UC-W1, UC-W2, ...
    title
    primaryActor
    trigger
    successGuarantee
    area
    status : covered, partial, missing
    change
  }
}

package "6. Assurance and docs: how we know and tell" <<Rectangle>> #ECEFF1 {
  class Test #CFD8DC {
    kind : probe, trigger-set, eval-case, gherkin, lint-check
  }
  class Doc #CFD8DC {
    door : install, use, develop
  }
  class Change #CFD8DC {
    epic
  }
}

' --- lane order (hidden) ---
Catalogue -[hidden]down- Skill
Skill -[hidden]down- Agent
Agent -[hidden]down- ExternalDependency
ExternalDependency -[hidden]down- UseCase
UseCase -[hidden]down- Test

' --- distribution ---
Catalogue "1" *-- "1..*" Bundle
Bundle "1" o-- "*" Skill : contains
Bundle "1" o-- "*" Agent : contains
Bundle "1" o-- "*" ConfigItem : ships
Bundle --> Bundle : requires
Binding --> Doc : routes to
ConfigItem ..> Skill : enforces a rule of

' --- knowledge ---
Skill "1" *-- "*" Resource : owns
Skill ..> Skill : requires by name
Skill "1" *-- "0..1" ToolPolicy : allowed-tools

' --- action ---
Agent --> "1..*" Skill : composes
Agent "1" *-- "1" DispatchContract
Agent "1" *-- "1" ToolPolicy : tools
Agent --> "1" Runtime : runs on
Agent ..> Agent : delegates to

' --- external ---
Skill --> "*" ExternalDependency : requires
Agent --> "*" ExternalDependency : requires
Bundle --> "*" ExternalDependency : declares
MemoryStore --|> ExternalDependency
Agent --> "*" MemoryStore : reads and writes

' --- intent ---
UseCase --> "*" Agent : served by
UseCase --> "*" Skill : needs

' --- assurance and docs ---
Test --> UseCase : accepts
Test --> Skill : proves
Test --> Agent : proves
Doc --> UseCase : narrates
Doc --> Skill : points to
Change --> UseCase : starts from
Change --> Skill : creates or changes
Change --> Agent : creates or changes

note right of Skill
  One concrete class; kind is open and conceptual
  (no frontmatter field until a check needs it).
  A foundation skill owns only shared resources.
  Folder anatomy: SKILL.md, references/,
  assets/, scripts/ (each file a Resource).
end note

note right of UseCase
  A White use case (Cockburn convention of
  the architecture skill): actor, trigger,
  success guarantee. Entry point for requirements;
  Gherkin is projected from it.
end note

note right of ConfigItem
  Keep in mind: hooks (hooks/inventory.yaml),
  commands, rules and settings that a bundle
  or a project's config folder may carry.
end note

legend right
  |= Lane |= Colour |
  | Distribution | <#BBDEFB> blue |
  | Knowledge | <#C8E6C9> green |
  | Action | <#FFE0B2> orange |
  | External | <#F8BBD0> pink |
  | Intent | <#E1BEE7> purple |
  | Assurance and docs | <#CFD8DC> grey |
  | new, later | deeper tint: added by the reshape, or kept in mind |
endlegend

@enduml
